# Ideable Project .gitignore
# Based on general-guidelines.md Version Control section

# ================================
# Agent-Generated Recap Files
# ================================
# Summary and guide files created by Antigravity agent
AGENT_RECAP/

# ================================
# Agent Runtime Artifacts
# ================================
# Per-developer Claude Code settings. Ignored HERE rather than left to a personal
# ~/.gitignore_global, because the dev tools container does not have that file: git inside the
# container saw this as untracked, `run_enabled_tests.sh` recorded `Working tree: dirty` on every
# run, and the push gate and `deliver` both read that field. One developer's personal config was
# deciding what the whole framework's runs claimed about themselves. Repo-local rules are the ones
# that are identical on every machine and inside the image — parity by construction, which is the
# reason the container exists at all.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Transient, machine-local lock/state files under .claude (e.g. scheduled_tasks.lock).
# These are runtime state, not framework files — never commit or propagate them.
.claude/*.lock


# ================================
# Agent-Skill repositories
# ================================
# Embedded git repositories for agent skills
.agent/checked-out/


# ================================
# Build Artifacts
# ================================
# DIST folders contain build/deployment artifacts
**/DIST/**
**/dist/
**/build/

# ================================
# Environment & Secrets
# ================================
# Secret files — do not commit
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.secrets
project.env
project.env.secrets

# Keep config and example files
!.env.config
!.env.config.example
!.env.secrets.example
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
!.env.*.template

# ================================
# Dependencies
# ================================
# Node.js
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
# package-lock.json is COMMITTED (Task 17c). Ignoring it meant every image build re-resolved
# the whole dependency tree from the registry, so an image tagged <commit> could not be
# rebuilt from <commit> — an immutable tag on a non-reproducible build is only half the
# property. See modules/host_app/SPECS/dependencies.md for the bump procedure.
yarn.lock

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
env/
venv/
ENV/
*.egg-info/
dist/
*.egg
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.tox/

# Java/Maven
target/
dependency-reduced-pom.xml
*.jar
!**/src/main/resources/**/*.jar
*.war
*.ear
*.class

